    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0226",
      "sequence": 238,
      "meaning": "At nightfall the sage gave leave and everyone performed the evening observance. As they told old histories, two watches of the lovely night passed. When the great sage went to rest, the two brothers began pressing his feet—those brothers, won over by love, tenderly massaged the guru’s lotus feet, though ascetics practicing many kinds of recitation, yoga and dispassion seek to touch their own lotus feet. The sage repeatedly ordered them to stop, and Raghubara at last went to bed. Lakṣmaṇa pressed the Lord’s feet and held them to his heart, receiving in reverence and love the highest joy. Again and again Rāma told the dear one to sleep; he lay down with the Lord’s lotus feet held in his heart. When the night was over, Lakṣmaṇa rose on hearing the rooster’s dawn-call. The wise lord of the world, Rāma, had awakened even before the guru.",
