    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0227",
      "sequence": 239,
      "meaning": "After completing every purification, the brothers went to bathe, performed their daily duties and bowed to the sage. Knowing the time and receiving the guru’s leave, they went to gather flowers. They came to see the king’s splendid garden, where enticing spring seemed to remain. Many kinds of captivating trees grew there, with awnings of vines in many colors; fresh leaves, fruits and lovely flowers put celestial trees to shame with their abundance. Cātakas, cuckoos, parrots and partridges called, and beautiful peacocks danced. In the garden’s middle shone a charming lake with wondrous jewel steps. Its pure water bore lotuses of many colors; waterbirds called and bees hummed. Seeing garden and pond, the Lord and his brother rejoiced: supremely lovely was the pleasure-ground that gave Rāma delight.",
