    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0228",
      "sequence": 240,
      "meaning": "Looking in all four directions and asking the gardeners, the brothers happily began gathering leaves and flowers. Just then Sītā came there, sent by her mother to worship Girijā. All her lovely, discerning companions sang in captivating voices. Near the lake stood Girijā’s beautiful shrine, indescribable and enchanting to behold. After bathing in the lake with her friends, Sītā went gladly into Gaurī’s sanctuary and worshipped with profound love, asking for a handsome bridegroom suited to herself. One companion left Sītā’s group to look at the flower garden. There she saw the two brothers and returned to Sītā, overwhelmed by love. Seeing her condition—body thrilled and eyes wet—the others gently asked the reason for her joy.",
