    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0229",
      "sequence": 241,
      "meaning": "‘Two princes have come to see the garden—adolescents beautiful in every way. One dark, one fair: how can I describe them? Speech has no eyes and eyes have no speech.’ Hearing this, the discerning companions rejoiced and recognized Sītā’s deep longing. One said, ‘Friend, they are surely the princes we heard arrived yesterday with the sage. Casting the enchantment of their beauty, they have brought every man and woman in the city under their power. Everyone everywhere describes their loveliness; they must be seen, for they are worthy of sight.’ These words delighted Sītā and her eyes grew restless for a glimpse. Placing that dear friend in front, she went on; no one perceived the ancient love. Remembering Nārada’s words, pure love arose in Sītā. Astonished, she searched every direction like a timid young doe.",
